  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "From the state Housing Element Annual Progress Report, through 2025.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001140",
        "SRC-001146"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City is reviewing plans for Phase 1 grading work.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001257"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "EIR summary: 87 attached townhomes in 17 clusters, three 2-, 3- and 4-bedroom designs of about 2,525 to 2,950 gross square feet each; about 1.4 of the 11.4 acres would remain undisturbed. EIR lists APNs 049-360-060, 050-220-020, 050-220-170 and 050-220-160 (800, 804, 806 and 808 Alameda de las Pulgas).",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003109"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "County parcel layer shows DRAGONFLY ASSETS C 56 LLC as owner of APNs 049-360-060 and 050-220-020 (804 Alameda de las Pulgas), as on the other two project parcels.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003113",
        "SRC-003112"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Palo Alto Daily Post (Dec 20, 2023): Veev, a Hayward prefabricated-housing company formerly known as Dragonfly Group, bought the Black Mountain site; it announced in late November 2023 that it was closing after a funding round fell through.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003110"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "White Oaks Blog (Dec 3, 2025): Lennar Corporation bought the project in 2023 after Veev's collapse; the developer still plans to break ground in 2026.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003111"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City page: Phase 1 grading covers tree and vegetation removal and rough grading for building pads near Alameda de las Pulgas; the existing on-site residences will be demolished. The adjacent 12-acre Vista del Grande site is not part of the project.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001257"
      ]
    }
  ],
